WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:05.760
Marvel isn't just telling a story in their
films, they're creating a whole universe.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.910
So if a character makes even the smallest
cameo in a movie, chances are there's a lot

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:12.420
more to them than we're seeing on-screen.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:16.930
Here's a spoiler-filled look at some characters
in Thor: Ragnarok with more meaning than you

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:18.860
might've realized.

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:19.860
Valkyrie

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.710
Movie fans around the world were thrilled
when they learned that the Hulk would be teaming

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.390
up with the God of Thunder in Thor: Ragnarok.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:30.980
But comic book fans were even more excited
to see the Hulk team up with the Marvel Cinematic

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:34.329
Universe's newest superheroine, Valkyrie.

00:00:34.329 --> 00:00:38.260
That's because Hulk and Valkyrie were friends
and teammates for years in the pages of the

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:43.870
classic Marvel series The Defenders, which
also featured Doctor Strange and the Sub-Mariner.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:47.739
While the Defenders name has been poached
by Marvel's TV division, seeing Valkyrie,

00:00:47.739 --> 00:00:52.449
Hulk, and Doctor Strange in the same movie
keeps the dream of a big-screen Defenders

00:00:52.449 --> 00:00:57.620
reunion alive, and further opens the door
for the eventual appearance of Namor in the

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:58.400
MCU.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:00:59.820
Grandmaster

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:05.160
Known across the galaxies as the Grandmaster,
En Dwi Gast is more than just a guy who loves

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:06.860
games and bloodsport.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:11.550
He's also one of the Elders of the Universe,
which, in Marvel Comics, is a group of immortal

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:16.480
beings of immense power who are traditionally
the guardians of the Infinity Stones.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:20.610
Like his fellow Elder, the Collector — who
was played by Benicio del Toro in Guardians

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:25.030
of the Galaxy — The Grandmaster is likely
to make another appearance when Thanos finally

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:28.530
rears his head in Avengers: Infinity War.

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:30.380
Skurge the Executioner

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:35.020
Hela's minion Skurge the Executioner has a
long and curious history in the comics.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:40.060
A longtime villain and adversary to Thor,
Skurge eventually redeemed himself in an epic

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:44.409
storyline, where he held off the armies of
Hell armed with a pair of machine guns in

00:01:44.409 --> 00:01:48.560
order to save Thor and a group of innocent
mortals fleeing from Hela.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:50.010
That part made it into the film.

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:55.040
But for most of his existence, it wasn't Hela
that Skurge was associated with, but rather

00:01:55.040 --> 00:02:00.300
his one true love, the immortal Asgardian
sorceress known as the Enchantress.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:05.530
Both an enemy and occasional ally of Thor,
the Enchantress is arguably the most important

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:09.330
character from Thor comics who hasn't yet
appeared in the MCU.

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:13.870
The appearance of Skurge in Thor: Ragnarok
suggests that might be on the verge of finally

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:15.090
changing.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:16.290
Korg

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:21.000
The rocklike Korg belongs to a species that
has actually been teased twice before in the

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:25.640
MCU, first in Thor: The Dark World, and then
again in a quick Easter egg in Guardians of

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:27.280
the Galaxy Vol. 2.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:31.560
And the character contains another secret,
as the CGI-created gladiator was played by

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:34.249
Thor: Ragnarok director Taika Waititi himself.

00:02:34.249 --> 00:02:39.659
But the real Easter egg behind Korg is a deep
cut from the very dawn of Marvel Comics: he's

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:45.319
part of the alien race originally known as
the "Stone Men from Saturn," who Thor fought

00:02:45.319 --> 00:02:50.469
in his very first comic book appearance in
1962's Journey into Mystery #83.

00:02:50.469 --> 00:02:55.409
In fact, in the comics, Korg himself is one
of the very alien invaders Thor battled in

00:02:55.409 --> 00:02:56.610
his origin story.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.360
How cool is that?

00:02:58.360 --> 00:02:59.360
Miek

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:03.709
Poor little Miek is played purely for comic
relief in Thor: Ragnarok, but in the comics

00:03:03.709 --> 00:03:05.340
he's a much darker figure.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:09.709
A lot of the plot of Thor: Ragnarok is borrowed
from the "Planet Hulk" comic book story, in

00:03:09.709 --> 00:03:14.099
which Hulk leads a band of fellow gladiators
on the planet Sakaar in a revolution.

00:03:14.099 --> 00:03:18.360
Hulk then becomes ruler of the planet, which
is where things take a sinister turn for Miek.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:23.150
Unsatisfied with the new peace Hulk has ushered
in, Miek is complicit in a plot that leads

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:28.310
to the death of Hulk's wife and child, sending
Hulk on a vengeful rampage across the galaxy.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:32.189
It's only later that Hulk discovers the base
treachery of his supposed friend.

00:03:32.189 --> 00:03:35.309
He doesn't seem so cute and goofy now, does
he?

00:03:35.309 --> 00:03:36.669
Topaz

00:03:36.669 --> 00:03:41.029
The Grandmaster's right-hand woman originally
wasn't even a Marvel character at all.

00:03:41.029 --> 00:03:46.129
Instead, she was created at Malibu Comics
as Queen Topaz, the ruler of a race of alien

00:03:46.129 --> 00:03:47.389
amazons.

00:03:47.389 --> 00:03:49.439
Eventually she ended up as a superhero on
Earth.

00:03:49.439 --> 00:03:53.319
After Marvel bought Malibu and folded some
of its characters into the Marvel Universe,

00:03:53.319 --> 00:03:58.029
she was summoned by the Grandmaster to be
a pawn in a contest with Loki, losing a fight

00:03:58.029 --> 00:04:00.730
against Crystal and Black Widow of the Avengers.

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:05.150
Topaz is the first Malibu character to make
it into the Marvel Cinematic Universe, opening

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:10.499
the door for characters like Hardcase, Firearm,
and Prime to potentially make the jump to

00:04:10.499 --> 00:04:12.449
the big screen as well.

00:04:12.449 --> 00:04:13.930
Beta Ray Bill

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:18.311
Eagle-eyed observers may have noticed that
one of the busts adorning the outside of the

00:04:18.311 --> 00:04:21.480
Grandmaster's tower is none other than Beta
Ray Bill himself.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:22.600
Who's that, you ask?

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:26.890
Well, you know that inscription on Thor's
hammer that says whoever is worthy can lift

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:29.130
the hammer and gain the power of Thor?

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:33.360
In the comics, Beta Ray Bill shocked Thor
and fans alike, by proving himself worthy

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:34.810
and lifting the hammer.

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:39.150
He became as powerful as Thor himself, and
earned the Thunder God's trust as his sworn

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:41.570
brother from an alien mother.

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:45.730
Beta Ray Bill has been a fan-favorite ever
since he first debuted in the early '80s,

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:49.260
so the fact that the film acknowledged his
existence is enough to send hardcore Thor

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.050
fans over the moon.

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:55.200
It means that somewhere out there in the MCU,
Beta Ray Bill exists.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:59.560
Now it's just a matter of actually putting
him into a movie, instead of just a statue

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:00.560
of his head.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:02.420
Are you listening, Marvel?

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:03.420
Thanks for watching!

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:06.070
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:08.220
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

